# AgX runtime tune:  E K S [shoulder]
#
# Copy to the game directory as `GP_agx.txt`. Hot-reloaded every 60 frames — you
# can edit it while the game runs and watch the change. Delete the file and the
# shader's baked-in defaults (0.55 / 1.40 / 1.20 / off) come back.
#
#   E         exposure fed into the AgX curve
#   K         contrast around mid-grey
#   S         saturation
#   shoulder  soft highlight knee, 0 = off. Values above it are compressed
#             asymptotically toward 1.0 instead of being hard-clipped; the cost
#             is that 1.0 itself maps to ~0.94, so a blown sky goes slightly grey.
#
# Why these knobs exist: the project's own A/B targets are contrast sigma
# 0.16-0.22, dark share 10-20%, saturation 15-25%, few clipped pixels. The
# shipped measurement was sigma 0.142, saturation ~15%, 15.4% overexposed — i.e.
# a touch soft, a touch desaturated, and clipping. The line below nudges contrast
# and saturation toward those targets without touching exposure:
#
#   K 1.40 -> 1.44 (+3%), S 1.20 -> 1.24 (+3%)
#
# Try in this order (one lap each, same spot/weather):
#   0.55 1.44 1.24 0            <- shipped starting point
#   0.55 1.48 1.28 0            <- closer to the targets
#   0.55 1.48 1.28 0.85         <- same, with highlight headroom
#   0.55 1.40 1.20 0            <- the old look, for comparison
#
# Measure with the existing tools instead of eyeballing:
#   python tools\grade_stats.py <before.png> <after.png>
0.55 1.44 1.24 0
